From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun8i: Enable jumbo frames up to MTU
 4070

The EMAC drops every frame longer than 1518 bytes (1522 with a VLAN
tag) as a length error, because EMAC_RX_CTL0 bit 29 (JUMBO_FRM_EN) is
never set. The Allwinner BSP driver sets it at init. Set it in
core_init, which also runs after the DMA reset of an MTU change. As on
dwmac4, longer frames from a link partner are then passed up at any
MTU.

Limit the MTU to 4070, so that a frame with two VLAN tags and the FCS
fits in the 4 KiB TX FIFO and is sent in store-and-forward mode (stmmac
selects it as tx_coe is set); stmmac_change_mtu() already refuses an
MTU above the TX FIFO size. Larger frames would need threshold mode.
With an earlier version of these patches, in threshold mode, the TX
FIFO underflowed now and then while the DMA moved a frame over several
descriptors: on an H616, 28 of 944 frames of 4110 to 16334 bytes were
lost. I have not found the cause.

Until the stmmac core allows jumbo MTUs with normal descriptors, the
maximum stays at 3712.

[backport to 7.3.3: context changes only]
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
index 33ec037..02f4634 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun8i.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
+#include <linux/if_vlan.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 
 extern int sunxi_get_soc_chipid(unsigned char *chipid);
@@ -221,6 +222,7 @@ static const struct emac_variant emac_variant_h6 = {
 
 /* Used in RX_CTL0 */
 #define EMAC_RX_RECEIVER_EN             BIT(31)
+#define EMAC_RX_JUMBO_FRM_EN		BIT(29)
 #define EMAC_RX_DO_CRC BIT(27)
 #define EMAC_RX_FLOW_CTL_EN             BIT(16)
 
@@ -230,6 +232,13 @@ static const struct emac_variant emac_variant_h6 = {
 /* TX checksum insertion corrupts longer frames, and others sent after them */
 #define EMAC_TX_COE_MAX_LEN	2032
 
+/* Frames must fit in the 4 KiB TX FIFO, to be sent in store-and-forward
+ * mode, with two VLAN tags and the FCS.
+ */
+#define EMAC_TX_FIFO_SIZE	4096
+#define EMAC_MAX_MTU		(EMAC_TX_FIFO_SIZE - ETH_HLEN - \
+				 2 * VLAN_HLEN - ETH_FCS_LEN)
+
 /* Used in EMAC_TX_FLOW_CTL */
 #define EMAC_TX_FLOW_CTL_EN             BIT(0)
 
@@ -658,6 +667,13 @@ static void sun8i_dwmac_core_init(struct mac_device_info *hw,
 
 	v = (8 << EMAC_BURSTLEN_SHIFT); /* burst len */
 	writel(v, ioaddr + EMAC_BASIC_CTL1);
+
+	/* Without JUMBO_FRM_EN, frames longer than 1518 bytes (1522 with a
+	 * VLAN tag) are dropped as length errors.
+	 */
+	v = readl(ioaddr + EMAC_RX_CTL0);
+	v |= EMAC_RX_JUMBO_FRM_EN;
+	writel(v, ioaddr + EMAC_RX_CTL0);
 }
 
 static void sun8i_dwmac_set_mac(void __iomem *ioaddr, bool enable)
@@ -1270,8 +1286,9 @@ static int sun8i_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	plat_dat->init = sun8i_dwmac_init;
 	plat_dat->exit = sun8i_dwmac_exit;
 	plat_dat->mac_setup = sun8i_dwmac_setup;
-	plat_dat->tx_fifo_size = 4096;
+	plat_dat->tx_fifo_size = EMAC_TX_FIFO_SIZE;
 	plat_dat->rx_fifo_size = 16384;
+	plat_dat->maxmtu = EMAC_MAX_MTU;
 
 	ret = sun8i_dwmac_set_syscon(&pdev->dev, plat_dat);
 	if (ret)
